# The spec of this round (scripts/gizmo-perf/gizmo-perf.spec.py) run against the runners of 3d5b436 (3d5b43627644860fccab5bf7128cd809fb98d7ad, the PR head the round started from):
# `git archive` of that commit (the WHOLE tree, 34 MB: the first attempt archived only scripts/gizmo-perf, the fixtures and measure-12bc8da and left THREE tests of the
# baseline failing for want of crates/ and the rest of the tree, so the whole tree was used, as in round 8) into a temp directory OUTSIDE the worktree, the new spec copied over its
# old one, `git init` and ONE commit of it (the spec runs git against a real repository). Nothing was linked from the worktree, nothing was written in it, no checkout or
# worktree was created (`target/` does not exist there: no editor binary, no build is possible).
# How it ran: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 collect.py scripts/gizmo-perf/gizmo-perf.spec.py OUT.json (cwd: that temp directory). collect.py (appendix at the end of this file) loads the spec
# file and runs its tests with a unittest.TestResult that records the outcome of every test, so that the per-test lists below are not parsed from text; it is the same suite as
# `python3 scripts/gizmo-perf/gizmo-perf.spec.py`, which the delivery report runs on the final tree.
# Python 3.14.3; git version 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155); worktree HEAD when it ran: 3d5b43627644860fccab5bf7128cd809fb98d7ad (3d5b436, the parent of the code commit), with the round-10 changes not yet committed.
# The files under test, by git blob id (the code commit holds these same blobs; 3d5b436 in parentheses):
#   scripts/gizmo-perf/gizmo-perf.spec.py     42478532c5a137c48be9ab9f041fc362b0c8d0b4 (55bd4e6a9e3f56001c57c883d7115d755b4e16f0)
#   scripts/gizmo-perf/native.py              8d1f949ecb7b713e246b64f788eca99192c0d41e (224c065896e9135c576f7d2d37ac8ccdb0844c38)
# harness.py, ab.py, run.py, mutate.py, audit.py, budgets.py and corpus.py are those of 3d5b436, byte for byte (checked with `diff -rq` between the two trees: only native.py differs).
# MACHINE LOAD (load averages 1/5/15 min): 31.52 23.66 23.31 at 15:53 (before the controls); 22.87 24.13 23.90 when the three whole-spec runs had finished (16:03); the wrong-fix runs followed. An unrelated heavy load stays on the machine.
# NOTHING WAS MEASURED: no time run, no A/B, no time mutant, no native window, no build, no performance lock, no benchmark, no real timing of anything.
# This is a test of the runners' bookkeeping on fakes under a VIRTUAL clock (a 60 s wait is read off the clock, not waited for), and on the pictures and hashes of the first real run's report
# (12bc8da, immutable evidence, read only). It says what the runners DO with those values; it does not say what the product does.
# The control, on the same layout:
#   old spec + OLD runners : Ran 254 tests in 62.4s -> OK  (the layout works)
#   new spec + OLD runners : Ran 285 tests in 62.1s -> FAILED (failures=30, errors=9; 26 tests with a failing assertion)
#   new spec + new runners : Ran 285 tests in 63.1s -> OK
# 31 tests are new in this round (ids that the spec of 3d5b436 does not have); 0 earlier id(s) were removed; the other 254 are the earlier ones.
# Per test: 26 of the 31 new tests fail on the old runners, 5 pass on both sides on purpose (listed after the list below), and 0 EARLIER tests fail on the old runners (no test was rewritten this round).
# The counts of unittest are per failing assertion (a failing subTest counts once each).
# Where the behaviour can be seen through `run_corpus` or `native.drag` the new test fails on its own assertion on the old runners; the tests that read `Undoable.committed_hash` (a field that did not exist)
# or `native.JOB_SECONDS` can fail there by not finding it. What proves that the tests also tell a right behaviour from a wrong one is the third part: deliberately WRONG versions of the fixes, each caught by at least one test.
# Labels: F2 = a final `job.get` answer that arrives after the 60 s deadline was accepted and `job.commit` was sent after it; (26a) = a redo was never compared with the commit's picture (hash recorded, never compared);
# (26b) = the two history stacks moved only when an undo drew a picture; sweep (c)/(a) = `settle_commit` refuses a late read (a branch the sweep found pinned by no test).

